# Plan (sonnet, medium)

## Goal

The Cards tab of `/stats` loses When drawn, Drawn vs not drawn, Radiant and Normal (columns, grid figures, toggles, sort options, "not enough data" cell). With **Show 95% ranges** on, each tier chip carries its fit %, the share of the Adjusted range inside the tier's band, computed in a new `tierFit.ts`. The Tier sort orders by tier, then fit %, then Adjusted. The Created cards table sorts by every header. Web and spec only; one ruling, R3184000, records it.

## Files to touch

| File | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/routes/stats.tsx` | change | remove the four columns; `TierFitText`; Tier sort's fit key |
| `apps/web/src/stats/tierFit.ts` | new | `tierBand`, `tierFit`, `cardTierFit` |
| `apps/web/src/stats/tierFit.test.ts` | new | unit tests |
| `apps/web/src/stats/CreatedPanel.tsx` | change | sortable headers |
| `apps/web/src/stats/CreatedPanel.test.tsx` | change | sort tests |
| `apps/web/src/stats/testids.ts` | change | `tierFit` id |
| `apps/web/src/stats/model.ts` | change | `faceRate` comment only |
| `apps/web/src/routes/stats.test.tsx` | change | replace tests of the four columns; add fit and tier-sort tests |
| `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` | change | one new entry |
| `spec/rulings/R3184000.md`, `spec/pending/3184.md` | new | the ruling; its §11 paragraph |
| `spec/09-architecture.md` | change | §9.11 `- **The breakdowns.**` and `- **Queries.**` bullets |
| `spec/rulings/R1147000.md`, `R2427000.md`, `R2089000.md`, `R2895000.md`, `R3022000.md` | change | amend prose; R1147000 and R2427000 lose `apps/web/src/routes/stats.test.tsx` from `proven_in` (it will hold no test of theirs) |

Do not touch: `crates/`, `apps/edge`, `apps/admin`, `e2e/`, `net/api.ts`, `wire/`, `CardStatsBlock*`, `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md` (never run `cargo jackioh spec index`), `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`.

Governing: SPEC §9.11; R654, R1147000, R2089000, R2427000, R2446000, R2895000, R3022000; CLAUDE.md rules 3, 7, 9.

## Steps

1. **`testids.ts`**: after `tiersNote` add `/** R3184000: a tier's fit % under its chip while ranges show. */ tierFit: "stats-tier-fit",`.

2. **`tierFit.ts`** (new). Header comment citing §9.11, R3184000, R2895000, R3022000. Imports `PublicCardStat`, `PublicStatsTiers` (`../net/api.ts`) and `CardTier` (`../wire/generated/CardTier.ts`).
```ts
const BAND_TIERS: readonly CardTier[] = ["A", "B", "C", "D"];
/** Unit conversion, not configuration: a share of 0..1 as a whole percent. */
const PERCENT = 100;
export function tierBand(tier: CardTier, bandLow: number, bandHigh: number): readonly [number, number] {
  if (tier === "S") return [bandHigh, Infinity];
  if (tier === "F") return [-Infinity, bandLow];
  const step = (bandHigh - bandLow) / BAND_TIERS.length;
  const top = bandHigh - BAND_TIERS.indexOf(tier) * step;
  return [top - step, top];
}
/** Share 0..1 of [low, high] inside the tier's band; zero width is its point, in (edges included) or out. */
export function tierFit(tier: CardTier, low: number, high: number, bandLow: number, bandHigh: number): number {
  const [from, to] = tierBand(tier, bandLow, bandHigh);
  if (high <= low) return low >= from && low <= to ? 1 : 0;
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(high, to) - Math.max(low, from)) / (high - low);
}
/** Whole percent, or null: below the floor, no tier, no Adjusted range, or no band (`tiers` absent). */
export function cardTierFit(card: PublicCardStat, tiers: PublicStatsTiers | undefined): number | null {
  if (!card.hasEnoughGames || !card.tier || !tiers) return null;
  if (typeof card.adjustedLow !== "number" || typeof card.adjustedHigh !== "number") return null;
  return Math.round(tierFit(card.tier, card.adjustedLow, card.adjustedHigh, tiers.bandLow, tiers.bandHigh) * PERCENT);
}
```

3. **`stats.tsx`**, in this order:
   - Header comment: drop the clause about Drawn vs not drawn and "not enough data" (R2427000); add that the Tier shows its fit while ranges show and the Created cards sort by header (R3184000).
   - Imports: delete `import { faceRate, formatPlayedDelta } from "../stats/model.ts";` (unused after this step); add `import { cardTierFit } from "../stats/tierFit.ts";` between the `testids.ts` and `TokensPanel.tsx` imports.
   - `SortColumn`, `SORT_COLUMNS`, `SORT_LABELS`: delete `drawnWinRate`, `drawnDelta`, `radiantWinRate`, `normalWinRate`. `sortOf` needs no code change (its `find` already yields the default); extend its comment to name the four.
   - After `RangeText` add:
```tsx
/** R3184000: under a tier chip, the share of the card's Adjusted range inside the tier; nothing when there is none. */
function TierFitText({ percent }: { percent: number | null }): ReactElement | null {
  if (percent === null) return null;
  return (
    <span className="stats-sample-hint stats-range" data-testid={statsTestid.tierFit} title={t("How much of the card's Adjusted 95% range lies inside its tier")}>
      {`${String(percent)}%`}
    </span>
  );
}
```
   - `visibleCols`: delete the four keys.
   - `filteredCards` sort: delete the four branches. In the `tier` branch, after `if (aRank !== bRank) return (aRank - bRank) * flip;` and before the adjusted-rate lines insert `const aFit = cardTierFit(a, tiers); const bFit = cardTierFit(b, tiers); if (aFit !== null && bFit === null) return -1; if (aFit === null && bFit !== null) return 1; if (aFit !== null && bFit !== null && aFit !== bFit) return (aFit - bFit) * flip;`. Update its comment (tier, fit, adjusted). Deps become `[cardStatsData, search, keywordFilter, sortCol, sortDir, locale, tiers]` (`minSample` out, `tiers` in; it is declared above).
   - Grid: delete the `radiant`/`normal` consts and the Radiant and Normal `<dt>/<dd>` pairs. After the Tier `<TierChip …/>` add `{showRanges && <TierFitText percent={cardTierFit(card, tiers)} />}`.
   - Table: delete the four `<th>`s, the four `<td>`s and the `radiantRate`/`normalRate` consts. Add the same line after the Tier chip, as its sibling (tests read the chip's text).
