I used `E2E_CHROME_PIN=0` locally. Without it, CI replaces a system Chrome 155 with Chrome for Testing 154.

## Done when

- [ ] `e2e/cypress/component/fx-gallery-captures.cy.tsx` and `e2e/cypress/component/fx-phone-frame.cy.tsx` are changed as above, and nothing else.
- [ ] `pnpm --dir e2e typecheck:component` and eslint on both files are clean.
- [ ] The two-spec run shows 40 of 40 passing.
- [ ] In the 4-way contention run, `shift` passes every time. A frame-budget failure in at most 1 of 4 is acceptable, because that load is artificial. Baseline was 2 of 4 failing; my hardened run had `shift` 0 of 4 and the Mythic budget 1 of 4 (52.7 ms on its last attempt).
- [ ] The pull request says that `e2e component (chrome)` is the job fixed, that a pull request's CI never runs it (only `workflow_dispatch` with `e2e: all` and the daily super run do), and that I checked by reproducing at `4c19b88` and the tip plus the contention runs above.
- [ ] Harness checks pass: rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings, clippy, cargo tests, web tests.

## Risks

- **The log may name a different failure.** If it shows `exceeded the maximum execution time of 20 minutes`, or a spec other than these two, this plan does not fix it.
  - **Hang:** one of my 3-way contended full runs froze for 15 minutes in `radiant-marks.cy.tsx` on a trivial test. That looks like a Chrome or Cypress stall under load, and no spec edit fixes it. If the log shows it, ask a person to raise `timeout-minutes: 20` at `.github/workflows/super.yml` line 318 and the same line in `ci.yml`'s `e2e-component`.
  - **Time:** the suite takes 8:19 to 8:55 of Cypress time on this 4-vCPU box, so 20 minutes is tight only on a slower runner.
- **Frame-budget threshold stays at 50 ms.** Retry-taking-the-best is the only change to the gate. A scene that is really slow fails all three windows. Do not swap the mean for a median or drop stalled frames. I checked that a long early stall would leave too few frames.
- **Observer state is kept on the window.** `watchGhosts` disconnects any earlier observer, so tests do not leak into each other.
- **Cypress queue order:** nested `holdsBudget` retries run before the trailing `[data-animating]` assertions. Do not move those assertions into the scene closure, because they would then run once per attempt.

## Open questions

- Which spec did the daily run actually fail on? Only the log (`gh run view 42054921295 --job 127350356723 --log-failed`) settles that. If it was neither of these two, or was a timeout, open a follow-up.
- `e2e/support/chrome-pin.ts` fetches Chrome for Testing with no timeout, and only when the system Chrome is 155. I left it alone because I found no evidence it is involved. Say so if you want it bounded.

